  "narrative": "No validation was requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted; remaining_new_requests is zero. All assessments below are therefore dataset-internal observational judgments. I evaluated the controller-supplied signed estimates and 95% Welch intervals against the +0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold in the registered direction. The signed estimates were used as provided; no direction multiplication was applied. I retained the conservative lower-bound convention for acceptance: accept when both the signed point estimate and signed lower bound clear +0.15; leave unresolved when the point estimate is suggestive but the interval does not clear the threshold or precision is inadequate; reject when the estimate is opposite the registered direction, clearly subthreshold, or too imprecise to support a meaningful effect. For H300, PTEN loss among cells with ifn_gamma_signature >= 0.75 gives a signed estimate +0.578 with lower bound +0.336 and upper bound +0.821, with adequate cell counts. Because the registered direction is -1, this corresponds to a raw lower composite score among PTEN-loss cells, i.e. stronger dependency association. I accepted this as a supported dataset-internal context effect. H301 gives the corresponding IFN>=0.75 interaction contrast, signed estimate +0.430, lower bound +0.167, upper bound +0.692, with all cells above the minimum count. This also clears the lower-bound threshold and supports the interpretation that, in this dataset, the PTEN-loss stronger-dependency association is elevated in high IFN relative to the complement. However, this remains a post hoc threshold-selected context discovered after many PTEN analyses, and independent validation is unavailable; it should be reported as an internal context-dependent association, not a generalizable mechanistic rule. H29 shows SMARCA4-loss stronger-dependency association within the matched RNA/DNA subset: signed estimate +0.831, lower bound +0.761, upper bound +0.901. This is far above threshold and closes the data-completeness robustness question consistently with the near-null has_matched_rna_dna main effect, although it does not rule out other correlated technical or biological confounders. H56 is PTEN loss in the Avana CRISPR library: signed estimate +0.248, lower bound +0.146, upper bound +0.351. The point estimate is meaningful, but the lower bound is just below +0.15. I therefore left it unresolved and closed rather than accepting a broad library-stratified PTEN effect. H299 tests the clean-background KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction restricted to SMARCA4-wild-type and PTEN-wild-type cells. The signed estimate is +0.154 but the lower bound is -0.051 and the interval includes zero. This does not support TP53 loss as an effect modifier of KEAP1 loss beyond their accepted main effects. It leaves the earlier suggestive but imprecise interaction unresolved and closes that residual question. H70 rejects the PTEN-by-lineage interaction: signed estimate -0.069, lower bound -0.293, upper bound +0.155. This is opposite the claimed direction and not compatible with a lineage-specific interaction under this threshold. H119, H185, H117, and H118 test modifier interactions for SMARCA4 loss by low 9p21 copy number, KEAP1 loss by MYC expression, KEAP1 loss by hypoxia, and TP53 loss by stemness. All are subthreshold or have intervals crossing zero: H119 signed +0.054 [-0.107,0.215], H185 signed +0.029 [-0.119,0.176], H117 signed +0.034 [-0.113,0.182], and H118 signed +0.145 [-0.054,0.343]. H118 is closest but the point estimate is below +0.15 and the lower bound is negative, so I rejected it rather than carrying it as a supported modifier. H71 and H123 assess APC mutation in opposite directions using the same evidence: signed estimates are +0.030 and -0.030 with intervals spanning zero. There is no evidence for a main APC effect in either direction. Overall, these new results do not add a new broad predictor. They confirm SMARCA4-loss robustness, strengthen the internal PTEN-loss IFN-high context, and close several interaction hypotheses as unsupported. The main dataset-internal supported axes remain SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency, KEAP1-loss weaker dependency, MSI-high stronger dependency, and TP53-loss weaker dependency. PTEN loss remains context-dependent, with accepted contexts now including broad IFN>=0.75. Important limitations remain: extensive multiplicity, correlated genomic and technical variables, no adjustment for competing predictors, unknown clustering, and the composite endpoint not representing a single-gene knockout measurement. Acceptance claims are not causal or externally generalizable.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 23 appraise. Validation budget exhausted; no validate request possible. Decision rule remained: accept only when signed estimate and signed 95% Welch lower bound exceed +0.15 in the claimed direction; reject null/subthreshold/opposite interactions; leave borderline interval cases unresolved when no validation capacity remains. New due assessments: H300 accepted, PTEN loss in IFN>=0.75 main contrast signed +0.578 lower +0.336. H301 accepted, PTEN loss IFN>=0.75 interaction signed +0.430 lower +0.167. H29 accepted, SMARCA4 loss in matched RNA/DNA signed +0.831 lower +0.761. H56 unresolved/closed, PTEN in Avana signed +0.248 lower +0.146, lower bound just below threshold. H299 unresolved/closed, clean-background KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction signed +0.154 lower -0.051, no supported interaction. H70 rejected, PTEN-by-lineage interaction negative. H117, H118, H119, H185 rejected, no supported hypoxia, stemness, low 9p21, or MYC modifier interaction. H71/H123 rejected, APC null. Controller accepted set updates by H29, H300, H301 acceptances and rejections/closures above. Final plan: stop exploratory subgroup scanning; synthesize as follows. Robust dataset-internal associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency; KEAP1 loss weaker dependency; MSI-high stronger dependency; TP53 loss weaker dependency. PTEN loss is not global but accepted in selected contexts including clean triple-negative adherent/adenocarcinoma settings, low aneuploidy, KEAP1-loss cells, PIK3CA-wild-type/high-IFN, and now broad IFN>=0.75. Constructed research markers, technical library/QC contrasts, APC, and tested modifier interactions are unsupported. Remaining uncertainty includes many heavily filtered PTEN/TP53 contexts and the KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction. All conclusions are observational, dataset-internal, multiplicity-limited, and not causal or external."
